      "title": "Syslog native workspace development fixture",
      "summary": "Private capability fixture, not a registered curriculum lab.",
      "objective": "Send the supplied warning event to Operations using facility23 (local7), keep debug detail out of the local and remote logs, and retain local warnings.",
      "retry_guidance": "Inspect the selected event severity, source export facility and collector selector. Apply pending settings before Check configuration. Old accepted log records do not settle the current check.",
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "minutes": 15,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied event and policy",
        "Edit and apply native source or collector settings",
        "Generate simulated evidence if useful",
        "Check the whole current configuration"
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "Facility23 and a remote threshold4 meet the assignment. A remote threshold7 also works when the collector threshold4 rejects debug. Different correct thresholds and extra unused selectors are accepted when both positive and negative event cases pass.",
      "hints": [
        "The LINK label is not the exported RFC facility; inspect both labels.",
        "A lower numeric threshold admits fewer less-urgent messages. Keep the warning while filtering debug."
      ],
